      "rationale": "The decomposition appropriately separates prior supported decision, recovery assignment, renewed commitment and application. The prior decision must retain ordered operation, key and value-byte contents independently of mutable instance fields. AcceptReply serializes only instance and ballot, whereas PrepareReply also carries AcceptorId and accepted-value information. Because handleAccept replies even after rejection or committed-instance preservation, distinct installation witnesses and their correlated replies are necessary; a matching counter alone is insufficient. Assignment preservation is sufficient only for this local boundary: other replacement paths, reply accounting and commit processing can still produce broader disagreement while this obligation holds. A finite next investigation is one instance and the three selected replicas: establish both original nonleader installations and replica 0's supported decision, pause its run goroutine before commit broadcast, reach replica 1's actual execution-gap recovery enqueue and dispatch, deliver replica 2's matching PrepareReply, and compare the threshold assignment with the retained decision contents. Stop the immediate check at that assignment; explore subsequent commitment and application separately. Preserve pending protective traffic and resume it when exploring those consequences. The supplied source is sufficient to specify this investigation without another repository read, but this reply cannot create an executable model, monitor or execution result.",
